<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Features</span>
            <h1>Moves for misc, reverse and forensics</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                OpenCTF is a CTF toolbox: every item below is backed by an operation
                the command line can run on a challenge file today. Anything outside
                that boundary is named as missing, not implied by a menu entry.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Containers</span>
                    <h2>Header decoding</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Detection is by magic bytes, never by file extension. Once a file is identified, <code>unpack</code> expands 7z, asar, NSIS and PyInstaller containers and <code>inflate</code> decodes zlib, gzip and raw DEFLATE streams.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-3">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <header>
                        <h3>Portable Executable</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">supported</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>DOS <code>MZ</code> stub and the <code>PE\0\0</code> signature.</li>
                        <li>PE32 and PE32+ headers, sections and the Rich header.</li>
                        <li>Imports, exports, delay imports, bound imports and debug entries.</li>
                        <li>Mitigations, resources, relocations, exceptions, TLS, certificates and load config.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <header>
                        <h3>ELF</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">supported</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>ELF32 and ELF64 little-endian files.</li>
                        <li>Interpreter, SONAME, NEEDED, RPATH and RUNPATH.</li>
                        <li>Segments, static symbols and notes such as the build id.</li>
                        <li>Big-endian files are rejected, not guessed.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card feature-card--quiet">
                    <header>
                        <h3>Mach-O</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--warn">supported</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Thin and fat/universal containers with slice listing.</li>
                        <li>Segments, sections, dylibs and the build version.</li>
                        <li>Symbol table, function starts and the export trie.</li>
                        <li>The code signature is reported, never verified.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Layout</span>
                    <h2>Section maps and address translation</h2>
                </div>
                <p>When a challenge names an address, the map stays checkable: each result is a number, not an interpretation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Field</th>
                            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
                            <th scope="col">Where it comes from</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">name</td>
                            <td>Section name, trimmed at the first NUL.</td>
                            <td>PE section table, ELF name table or Mach-O section</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">virtualAddress</td>
                            <td>RVA for PE, virtual address for ELF.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">virtualSize</td>
                            <td>Resident size in memory.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">rawPointer</td>
                            <td>File offset of the section data.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">rawSize</td>
                            <td>Number of bytes stored on disk.</td>
                            <td>Section header</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="mono">readable / writable / executable</td>
                            <td>Access flags decoded from the flag word.</td>
                            <td>PE characteristics or ELF <code>sh_flags</code></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="section-note">
                <code>open-ctf rva</code> maps an address onto a file offset, and
                <code>open-ctf offset</code> walks the other way from a file offset
                to an RVA and virtual address. A value in zero-filled memory or
                outside every section is rejected with <code>binary/range</code>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Reading</span>
                    <h2>Strings, hex, searches and entropy</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Four views of the same bytes, each with an explicit bound — plus <code>disasm</code> when the range is code.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-2">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Printable runs and pattern hits</h3>
                    <p>
                        Strings come back as printable ASCII or UTF-16LE runs with
                        their file offset and byte length, defaulting to a minimum of
                        four and a limit of one hundred. <code>search</code> matches
                        hex, ASCII or UTF-16LE, and <code>find</code> takes a byte
                        regex over the whole file.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Canonical dump and entropy</h3>
                    <p>
                        The hex dump keeps the familiar
                        <code>offset  bytes  |ascii|</code> layout, sixteen bytes per
                        row. <code>entropy</code> reports whole-file and per-section
                        values plus the PE overlay, usually the first thing to check
                        when a challenge file looks packed.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Writing</span>
                    <h2>A patch you can audit</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Nothing is written until the whole range fits the file, and <code>diff</code> shows what moved between two builds first.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="detail-list">
                <li><b>Validate.</b> The offset and length are checked against the file size first.</li>
                <li><b>Stage.</b> Patched bytes go to a sibling temporary file in the same directory.</li>
                <li><b>Rename.</b> The temporary file replaces the target, so a partial write is never visible.</li>
                <li><b>Report.</b> The result carries the target path, offset, length and the whole-file XXH64 hash before and after.</li>
                <li><b>Keep the source.</b> Pass an output path and the opened file is left untouched.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Surfaces</span>
                    <h2>One engine, three callers</h2>
                </div>
                <p>The CLI, the studio and the agent skill consume the same reports.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-3">
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Command line</h3>
                    <p><code>info</code>, <code>strings</code>, <code>entropy</code>, <code>unpack</code>, <code>disasm</code>, <code>carve</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>dump</code>, <code>diff</code>, <code>patch</code> and <code>capabilities</code>, plus format-specific fact commands for PE, ELF and Mach-O.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Studio</h3>
                    <p>The window reads the same handles over its bridge. Without a host it shows a disconnected state and no sample data.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <h3>Agent skill</h3>
                    <p>The skill document repeats the implemented routes and the hard rules: no invented sections, no unverified patches.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Contract</span>
                    <h2>Errors that can be compared</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Every failure carries a stable code, so callers never parse prose.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Code</th>
                            <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/parse</td><td>The container is recognised but its header or table is malformed.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/range</td><td>An offset, length, RVA or patch target is outside the file.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/unsupported</td><td>The operation is not implemented for this container.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">binary/io</td><td>The file could not be read or written.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">handle/invalid</td><td>No open file has that handle.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td class="mono">capability/not-implemented</td><td>No engine is connected, or the requested feature is not wired.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Honesty</span>
                    <h2>Not in this build</h2>
                </div>
                <p>These are absent by design, not hidden behind a disabled button with fake output.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="missing-list">
                <li>Decompilation, pseudo-code, control-flow graphs and type recovery.</li>
                <li>A debugger, breakpoints or process attachment.</li>
                <li>Signature verification. Presence is reported, Authenticode is never validated.</li>
                <li>Disassembly outside x86 and x64.</li>
                <li>Mach-O runtime bindings and rebase streams.</li>
                <li>Big-endian ELF and byte orders the header does not report.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-band">
            <div>
                <h2>Check the boundary yourself</h2>
                <p><code>open-ctf capabilities</code> is the source of truth for what this build implements.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cta-band__actions">
                <Link to="RoadmapPage" class="btn btn--primary">
                    Roadmap
                </Link>
                <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://github.com/nyar-os/OpenCTF" rel="noopener">
                    Source
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </SiteShell>
</template>

